Fire the Lua fallback when Hyprland answers "unknown request"

hypr-rdp creates a headless output and then sets its resolution with
Hyprland's legacy `keyword` IPC request. Hyprland 0.56 dropped that request
for the Lua config, so the daemon dies at startup:

    failed to initialize display capture
      0: failed to set headless output resolution
      1: Hyprland IPC error: unknown request

keyword_monitor() already has the right fallback -- it translates the rule to
`hl.monitor({...})` and sends it through `eval` -- and it never fires, because
is_non_legacy_parser_error() matches only the string "non-legacy parsers"
while 0.56 answers "unknown request".

Verified on Hyprland 0.56.0 that the fallback itself is correct:

    $ hyprctl keyword monitor "HEADLESS-1,1920x1080@60,auto,1"
    unknown request
    $ hyprctl eval 'hl.monitor({ output = "HEADLESS-2", mode = "1920x1080@60", position = "auto", scale = 1 })'
    ok
      HEADLESS-2  1920x1080@60.0  scale=1

which is exactly what monitor_rule_to_lua() generates. So this widens the
matcher, adds a test beside upstream's two that pins the new message, and
changes nothing else.

Carried here rather than fixed upstream, which is the wrong way round and is
recorded as such: v0.1.6 is the newest tag and the narrow matcher is still on
upstream main. Drop this patch as soon as a release carries the fix --
olafkfreund/nixarchy#1031 tracks it.

--- a/src/hyprland.rs
+++ b/src/hyprland.rs
@@ -250,7 +250,14 @@
 fn is_non_legacy_parser_error(error: &anyhow::Error) -> bool {
     error
         .chain()
-        .any(|cause| cause.to_string().contains("non-legacy parsers"))
+        .any(|cause| {
+            let text = cause.to_string();
+            // Hyprland 0.56 dropped the legacy `keyword` request entirely and
+            // answers "unknown request"; older versions refused it with a
+            // message naming non-legacy parsers. Both mean the same thing:
+            // send the Lua form instead.
+            text.contains("non-legacy parsers") || text.contains("unknown request")
+        })
 }
 
 fn monitor_rule_to_lua(rule: &str) -> Result<String> {
@@ -603,6 +610,13 @@
 
         assert!(is_non_legacy_parser_error(&err));
     }
+
+    #[test]
+    fn non_legacy_parser_error_detection_matches_unknown_request() {
+        let err = anyhow!("Hyprland IPC error: unknown request");
+
+        assert!(is_non_legacy_parser_error(&err));
+    }
 
